    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70837" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῑκάτωρ</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾱ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ορος</span>, ὁ, 
			Dor.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νικήτωρ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>conqueror,</i> cult-name of
			Seleucus I and Demetrius, kings of Syria, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				233
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Arist.</u>
				6
			</span></i> (pl.), etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σέλευκος Ζεὺς Νικάτωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					245.11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in pl.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν., οἱ,</span>
			<i>the evervictorious,</i> epith. of the royal Macedonian
			bodyguard, Liv.<i><span class="en">
				43.19
			</span></i>.</div>
